# UX and accessibility

- Match existing TripTiles components, spacing and type before introducing a new visual pattern.
- Compare with Figma only after the Figma MCP connection is actually authenticated. Do not edit Figma files.
- Provide visible labels for inputs. Keep keyboard access for buttons, dialogs and day navigation.
- Do not rely on colour alone for crowd, wait or error status.
- Every changed screen needs a loading, empty and error state where data can fail.
- Do not describe static monthly weather as live weather, or stale waits as live waits.
